            <ArticleTitle>Long-term medical complications of heart transplantation: information for the primary care physician.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>673-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As heart transplantation becomes much more common primary care physicians will play a key role in preventing, detecting, and treating the short-term and long-term complications of this procedure. These complications include chiefly graft rejection and accelerated coronary artery disease, but also dyslipidemia, hypertension, diabetes mellitus, kidney failure, gout, osteoporosis, and malignancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
